  "answer": {
    "What this is": [
      "This is a folder of results from one sequencing run. NGS-Agent checks the files inside it against each other.",
      "Bottom line: Fix this and re-run. 1 of the 1 findings need the run to be fixed and repeated; nothing here is a judgement call."
    ],
    "What matters": [
      "Problem \u2014 Reads and gene annotation are naming chromosomes differently.",
      "    What it is: Only 18% of reads were assigned to genes. The aligned reads name their chromosomes like '1', but the gene list used for counting names them like 'chr1'.",
      "    What it means: The aligner and the gene annotation are working from two different dictionaries of chromosome names, so most reads have no gene to be counted against. Every step reported success, which is exactly why this one gets published by mistake: the counts are real numbers describing almost nothing. Differential expression from this run would be meaningless."
    ],
    "What to do": [
      "1. Re-run quantification using the annotation that matches the genome the reads were aligned to (same source, same chromosome naming). You do not need to re-align."
    ],
    "Receipts": [
      "AUD-STRAND-01: rule:AUD-STRAND-01 @ bam contigs vs annotation contigs, assignment rate \u2014 AUD-STRAND-01 evaluated against bam contigs vs annotation contigs, assignment rate",
